    {
      "name": "AuthorNotes",
      "type": "comment",
      "node_position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -250
      },
      "title": "Editable source artwork",
      "size": {
        "x": 820,
        "y": 300
      },
      "text": "Generated terrain/volcano pigment for the Classic column walls; it replaces the Enhanced terrain/surfaces/volcano-basalt map that the Classic walls borrowed. sources/pigment.png is a 512 px tileable source: Codex image generation from a Classic-style brief (references: the Classic rock, sand and dirt walls and the Classic volcano theme hexes), then, in linear light, an area resample to 512 px, periodic-plus-smooth seam correction, low-frequency lighting flattened and the mean albedo matched to the Classic volcano theme hexes. Hue, saturation and value are explicit author controls. Linear filtering occurs after one sRGB decode: LinearReduce averages each 4x4 block of source texels onto the 128 px grid, then one encode for the exported game PNG. This existing consumer uses RGB only; it has no height/normal/AO/roughness image input. The project therefore exports only the channel the game consumes. Save, export (target MegaMek/Maps), store the PNG as 8-bit RGB, then use the existing Reload Assets button."
    },
